[size=6][b]Gear Without Levels — for SpaceBourne 2[/b][/size]

In SpaceBourne 2 a weapon or suit above your character level cannot be equipped ("High Level"). That is an MMO rule: a better rifle does not need a level. What a rookie lacks is familiarity with advanced kit.

[b]Gear Without Levels[/b] removes the level lock for weapons, melee weapons and suits. Kit above your level always works, but handles a little worse until you have the experience for it:

[list]
[*]firearms kick a bit more per shot (up to +40 %);
[*]melee weapons cost a bit more stamina per swing (up to +25 %);
[*]an advanced suit tires you a bit faster when sprinting or swinging (up to +20 %).
[/list]

The penalty depends on how far above you the item is, on a log scale: an item at twice your level gives about half of it, the ±2 levels of normal loot give almost nothing, and a veteran adapts faster than a rookie. [b]Training[/b] helps too: rounds fired with a gun, swings with a blade and exertion in a suit make you familiar with that item and remove up to three quarters of its penalty before you level up. Damage, protection and rate of fire are [b]never[/b] changed.

The mod changes no items and nothing in your saves. Gear you equipped with it stays equipped if you remove it later.

[line]
[size=5][b]Install[/b][/size]

Needs [b]UE4SS[/b], a free script loader for Unreal Engine games. If you already play with [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-HardcoreTacticalRealism]Hardcore Tactical Realism[/url] or SB2 HOTAS, you have it.

[list=1]
[*]Download GearWithoutLevels-x.y.z.zip from [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-GearWithoutLevels/releases/latest]Releases[/url] or [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/7]Nexus Mods[/url].
[*]Open your game folder (...\SpaceBourne 2, the one with SpaceBourne2.exe) and extract the zip [b]there[/b]. It creates SB2\Binaries\Win64\Mods\GearWithoutLevels and switches itself on (enabled.txt).
[*]No UE4SS yet? Get [url=https://github.com/UE4SS-RE/RE-UE4SS/releases/tag/v3.0.1]RE-UE4SS 3.0.1[/url] and copy dwmapi.dll, UE4SS.dll and UE4SS-settings.ini into SpaceBourne 2\SB2\Binaries\Win64\.
[/list]

[b]Uninstall:[/b] delete the GearWithoutLevels folder.

[line]
[size=5][b]Controls[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Shift+Delete[/b] switches the mod on/off in game (remembered between sessions). The mod is [b]off[/b] until you switch it on (or set Enabled = true in scripts/config.lua).
[*]A short message on screen confirms the switch and tells you when you equip unfamiliar kit, for example "Unfamiliar suit (L12, you L5): 18% worse until trained". It stays 6 seconds, without a beep.
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]Settings (scripts/config.lua)[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Penalty — strength per kit type (recoil, melee stamina, suit stamina) and how fast the penalty grows with the level gap.
[*]Training — rounds, swings and stamina bars for full familiarity; how much training can remove (default 75 %).
[*]Unlock.PickLists — show over-level items in the character screen's item picker.
[*]Unlock.ShopShowsAllLevels — make the shop's "show unusable" filter treat every item as usable.
[*]Standalone.DamageCapLevels — used only without Hardcore Tactical Realism (below).
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]With Hardcore Tactical Realism[/b][/size]

Built as a companion to [b]Hardcore Tactical Realism (HTR)[/b], where damage depends on calibre, armor and hit zone instead of item level. With HTR's optional gear bonus (F8) on, an over-level weapon still gives its small HTR bonus (up to +8 penetration, +15 % damage at level 60), so the result is a [b]minor bonus with a small handling cost[/b].

Without HTR, vanilla weapon damage grows a lot with item level (×3.7 from level 10 to 40), so this mod caps an over-level gun to the damage of a gun 5 levels above you. It never becomes an exploit.

[line]
[size=5][b]Part of the SpaceBourne 2 realism set[/b][/size]

This mod is part of the realism set, built around [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/4]Hardcore Tactical Realism[/url] as the core mod. HTR is not required: this mod works on its own or with any of the others. [b]Install them all at once[/b] with the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/11]SpaceBourne 2 Realism installer[/url] ([url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-Realism]GitHub[/url]): tick the mods you want, and it switches them on and keeps them up to date.

[list]
[*][b]Hardcore Tactical Realism (HTR)[/b]: the core: realistic ballistics, wounds and tactical AI. [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-HardcoreTacticalRealism]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/4]Nexus[/url] · [url=https://steamcommunity.com/app/1646850/discussions/0/573805072991123580/]Steam[/url]
[*][b]Split Controls[/b]: separate look inversion for ships and on foot. [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-SplitControls]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/5]Nexus[/url]
[*][b]Silent Ops[/b]: realistic stealth, suppressors and silent takedowns. [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-SilentOps]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/6]Nexus[/url]
[*][b]Gear Without Levels[/b] [i](this mod)[/i]: any weapon or suit at any level, with small penalties. [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-GearWithoutLevels]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/7]Nexus[/url]
[*][b]SB2 HOTAS[/b]: joystick, HOTAS, pedals, head tracking and triple screen. [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-HOTAS]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/8]Nexus[/url]
[*][b]Faction Power[/b]: dungeons, sales and missions earn your faction power. [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-FactionPower]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/9]Nexus[/url]
[*][b]Tactical Engineering[/b]: deployable turrets and barricades that take time to set up. [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-TacticalEngineering]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/10]Nexus[/url]
[*][b]Ammo Discipline[/b]: realistic ammo limits and scavenging. [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-AmmoDiscipline]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/12]Nexus[/url]
[*][b]Ground Waypoints[/b]: planet waypoints on foot and on the hoverbike. [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-GroundWaypoints]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/13]Nexus[/url]
[*][b]Get Out of the Way[/b]: NPCs step aside naturally when you walk through them. [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-GetOutOfTheWay]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/14]Nexus[/url]
[/list]

Coming soon: Tactical First Person.

